Z||000000||Ed||06-26-2001||04:42 PM||||The car's in the shop getting fixed.  I was wondering if anyone knows how to remove the instructional decals for tire jacking, etc., on the underside of the front deck/hood? <P>Or are replacements available anywhere?<P>Trying to keep it as original as possible under the circumstances.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||06-26-2001||05:32 PM||||I suppose you could use a heat gun.  If you're careful(patient), you can avoid melting it and possibly save it.  The glue <I>should</I> soften up enough to sneak a sharp putty knife under it before the sticker starts to stretch or melt.  I wonder if you started an edge of it up that a product like Goo Gone could do the rest?????  Good luck anyway.  It sounds like a real time consumer to save the original sticker.  The sticker may be available through the dealership.  Stranger things have happened.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||06-26-2001||07:51 PM||||Hope you get it back soon Ed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>If you find that the dealer still has these let us know, or anyone that makes the factory stickers.  I know where to get them for my Camaros and most any chevy. But thats part of the game we play with our Little Toys<P>Good Luck with the repairs!!!!<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
